<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  kb-browser - the knowledge stack's headless-browser collector: Chromium (Microsoft's stock
  Playwright image) that opens a fund sponsor's script-rendered notice list and saves the notice
  PDFs into the knowledge base's drop folder, where kb-service picks them up. It is idle until
  run. Nothing here is specific to any host or operator.

  WHAT IT DOES AND DOES NOT DO. It checks robots.txt first, waits at least 5 seconds between
  requests, and stops completely at the first bot challenge, 403, 429 or 5xx. It never tries to
  pass a bot check.

  HOW IT RUNS. The container only sleeps (Post Arguments "sleep infinity"). A collection is
  started from outside with: docker exec <container> python /app/collect.py <sponsor>
  The script is NOT in the image: the Collector path below mounts the folder that holds
  collect.py read-only at /app.

  HARDENING. Extra Parameters ships empty (repo rule). After import, add these docker run
  options (each begins with two dashes, the two -e entries are environment variables):
  user 99:100; read-only; tmpfs /tmp:size=256m; shm-size=512m; cap-drop=ALL; security-opt
  no-new-privileges; cpus=1; memory=1g; -e HOME=/tmp; -e PYTHONPATH=/app/site
  It gives: a non-root user, a read-only root with RAM scratch for /tmp, the shared memory
  Chromium needs, all capabilities dropped, no new privileges, CPU and memory caps. No Docker
  socket, not privileged. PYTHONPATH names the folder under /app that holds the Python
  packages the collector imports.

  NETWORK. Put it on the same user-defined network as kb-service (the operator creates it once
  and sets the Network field; every template here keeps Network bridge). No port is published
  and there is no Port config. It needs outbound internet to the sponsor's site.

  START ORDER. After kb-service (the last group of the kb stack); it needs nothing from the
  stack to start, only the drop folder to exist.

  THE IMAGE TAG IS A FULL RELEASE (vX.Y.Z-noble), so the browser and the Python Playwright
  package inside move only when this tag is deliberately changed.
-->
<Container version="2">
  <Name>kb-browser</Name>
  <Repository>mcr.microsoft.com/playwright/python:v1.52.0-noble</Repository>
  <Registry>https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/playwright/python</Registry>
  <Network>bridge</Network>
  <MyIP/>
  <Shell>bash</Shell>
  <Privileged>false</Privileged>
  <Support>https://github.com/microsoft/playwright-python/issues</Support>
  <Project>https://github.com/microsoft/playwright-python</Project>
  <Overview>Headless Chromium collector for the knowledge base: opens a sponsor's script-rendered notice list and saves the notice PDFs into the drop folder. robots.txt first, at least 5 s between requests, full stop at the first challenge, 403, 429 or 5xx; it never tries to pass a bot check. Idle until run: docker exec the container with python /app/collect.py and the sponsor name. Needs the Collector folder (holds collect.py) and the Inbox folder.</Overview>
  <Description>Idle headless-browser collector for the knowledge base's fund notices; run on demand with docker exec.</Description>
  <Category>Productivity: Tools:Utilities</Category>
  <WebUI/>
  <TemplateURL>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sdr-ventures/unraid-templates/main/templates/kb-browser.xml</TemplateURL>
  <Icon>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sdr-ventures/unraid-templates/main/icons/kb-browser.png</Icon>
  <PostArgs>sleep infinity</PostArgs>
  <ExtraParams/>
  <DateInstalled/>
  <Config Name="Collector" Target="/app" Default="" Mode="ro" Description="REQUIRED. Folder on the host that holds collect.py, mounted read-only." Type="Path" Display="always" Required="true" Mask="false"></Config>
  <Config Name="Inbox" Target="/inbox" Default="" Mode="rw" Description="REQUIRED. The knowledge base's fund drop folder, the same folder kb-service reads (its KB_FUND_INBOX path, for example a fund_inbox folder under its assets)." Type="Path" Display="always" Required="true" Mask="false"></Config>
</Container>
